---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith('/') ? rawBase : rawBase + '/';
---

<Base title="How It Works — SkillSign">
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1 class="heading-xl">How It Works</h1>
    <p class="text-muted header-subtitle">
      SkillSign uses Sigstore keyless signing to bind your GitHub identity to your SKILL.md files
      without managing long-lived private keys.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Signing Flow -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <h2 class="heading-lg">Signing Flow</h2>
      <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom: var(--bh-spacing-8);">
        The signing protocol produces a detached sidecar file containing the signature,
        certificate, and transparency log entry. The SKILL.md file is never modified.
      </p>

      <bh-accordion>
        <bh-accordion-item label="1. Read the manifest" open>
          <p>
            The CLI reads <code class="code-inline">skillsign.yaml</code> from the same directory as the
            SKILL.md file. This manifest declares the skill's <code class="code-inline">skill_id</code>
            (e.g., <code class="code-inline">github.com/org/skill-name</code>) and
            <code class="code-inline">skill_version</code>. Both fields are validated — the skill_id must
            follow the <code class="code-inline">{'{host}/{owner}/{name}'}</code> format with ASCII-only characters.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="2. Check for existing sidecar">
          <p>
            If a <code class="code-inline">.skillsign</code> sidecar already exists for this skill_id
            and version, the CLI exits with code 10 unless <code class="code-inline">--force</code> is
            passed. This prevents accidental re-signing of the same version with a different key.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="3. Compute canonical form">
          <p>
            The SKILL.md file is normalized to a deterministic byte representation:
          </p>
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li>File size check (max 1MB)</li>
            <li>UTF-8 validation, BOM stripping</li>
            <li>Line ending normalization (CRLF → LF)</li>
            <li>Trailing whitespace stripping per line</li>
            <li>Single trailing newline</li>
            <li>Null byte rejection</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--bh-spacing-2);">
            This ensures trivial formatting differences don't break signatures while meaningful
            content changes always invalidate them.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="4. Compute SHA-256 digest">
          <p>
            The digest is computed over a structured byte sequence that binds the canonical content
            to the skill's identity:
          </p>
          <div class="code-block" style="margin: var(--bh-spacing-4) 0;">
"skillsign:v1" + \x00 + canonical_bytes + \x00 + skill_id + \x00 + skill_version</div>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The domain separator prevents cross-protocol confusion. Including skill_id and version in
            the digest prevents substitution attacks.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="5. Authenticate via OIDC">
          <p>
            The signer authenticates with GitHub via OIDC. In interactive mode, this opens a browser.
            In CI (GitHub Actions), ambient OIDC credentials are detected automatically.
            The result is an OIDC identity token proving the signer's GitHub identity.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="6. Obtain Fulcio certificate">
          <p>
            The OIDC token is submitted to Sigstore's Fulcio CA, which issues a short-lived X.509
            certificate (~10 minutes) binding an ephemeral ECDSA P-256 keypair to the signer's
            verified GitHub identity. The certificate's Subject Alternative Name (SAN) encodes the identity.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="7. Sign the digest (ECDSA P-256)">
          <p>
            The 32-byte SHA-256 digest is signed directly with the ephemeral private key using ECDSA P-256.
            The signature is computed over the raw digest bytes without re-hashing (prehash mode).
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="8. Record in Rekor transparency log">
          <p>
            The signature, certificate, and digest are submitted to Rekor as a
            <code class="code-inline">hashedrekord/v0.0.1</code> entry. Rekor returns a log entry ID,
            timestamp, and Signed Entry Timestamp (SET). The sidecar is only written after Rekor confirms.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="9. Write sidecar, discard key">
          <p>
            The sidecar YAML file (<code class="code-inline">SKILL.md.skillsign</code>) is written with
            all fields: version, skill_id, skill_version, signer, timestamps, digest, Rekor metadata,
            certificate, and signature. The ephemeral private key is discarded — it can never be used again.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>
      </bh-accordion>
    </div>
  </section>

  <bh-divider spacing="lg"></bh-divider>

  <!-- Verification Flow -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <h2 class="heading-lg">Verification Flow</h2>
      <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom: var(--bh-spacing-8);">
        Verification checks the signature, certificate chain, signer identity, and optionally
        enforces a trust policy. Each failure produces a specific result code.
      </p>

      <bh-accordion>
        <bh-accordion-item label="1. Locate and parse sidecar" open>
          <p>
            The CLI looks for <code class="code-inline">&lt;filename&gt;.md.skillsign</code> adjacent
            to the SKILL.md file. If no sidecar exists, the result is <code class="code-inline">UNSIGNED</code>
            (exit code 2). The sidecar is parsed as YAML 1.2 with strict restrictions: no duplicate keys,
            no anchors/aliases, no tags, max 64KB.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="2. Recompute digest">
          <p>
            The canonical form is recomputed from the current SKILL.md file, and the SHA-256 digest
            is calculated over the same structured byte sequence used during signing.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="3. Verify digest match">
          <p>
            The freshly computed digest is compared against the <code class="code-inline">digest</code>
            field in the sidecar. A mismatch means the file was modified after signing →
            <code class="code-inline">TAMPERED</code> (exit code 1).
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="4. Verify ECDSA signature">
          <p>
            The cryptographic signature is verified against the certificate's public key, using the
            freshly computed digest (not the sidecar's digest field). This ensures the signature
            was produced by the holder of the certificate's private key.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="5. Verify certificate chain">
          <p>
            The certificate chain is validated against the Sigstore TUF root to confirm it was
            issued by Fulcio. The Extended Key Usage (EKU) must include
            <code class="code-inline">id-kp-codeSigning</code>. In offline mode, the bundled
            TUF root is used.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="6. Verify signer identity (SAN match)">
          <p>
            The certificate's Subject Alternative Name is compared against the
            <code class="code-inline">signer</code> field in the sidecar. The match is case-sensitive
            and exact. URI SANs are used for GitHub identities; email SANs for personal OAuth.
            A mismatch → <code class="code-inline">IDENTITY_MISMATCH</code> (exit code 1).
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="7. Verify temporal validity (SET)">
          <p>
            The Rekor Signed Entry Timestamp (SET) is verified against Rekor's public key,
            then its embedded timestamp is checked against the certificate's validity window.
            This proves signing occurred while the certificate was valid — without needing
            a live Rekor query.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="8. Strict mode checks (optional)">
          <p>
            With <code class="code-inline">--strict</code>, the CLI additionally confirms the
            <code class="code-inline">rekor_log_id</code> exists in Rekor as a
            <code class="code-inline">hashedrekord/v0.0.1</code> entry and the entry's digest matches.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="9. Owner-path consistency check">
          <p>
            The <code class="code-inline">skill_id</code> owner path is compared against the
            <code class="code-inline">signer</code> owner path. For example, a skill at
            <code class="code-inline">github.com/org/skill</code> signed by
            <code class="code-inline">https://github.com/different-org</code> triggers
            <code class="code-inline">SKILL_ID_MISMATCH</code>. This can be downgraded to a
            warning via <code class="code-inline">--allow-id-mismatch</code>.
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>

        <bh-accordion-item label="10. Apply trust policy (optional)">
          <p>
            If a <code class="code-inline">.skillsign-policy.yaml</code> is provided via
            <code class="code-inline">--policy</code>, the policy engine evaluates rules
            (allowed signers, orgs, max age) after cryptographic verification. Policy failures
            produce <code class="code-inline">POLICY_FAIL</code> (exit code 3).
          </p>
        </bh-accordion-item>
      </bh-accordion>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Verification Results -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <h2 class="heading-lg">Verification Results</h2>
      <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom: var(--bh-spacing-8);">
        Every verification attempt produces one of these results, each with a specific exit code
        for CI integration.
      </p>

      <bh-grid gap="md" min="320px">
        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="success">Exit 0</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">VERIFIED</span>
          </div>
          Signature valid, signer identity confirmed, content unmodified.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="danger">Exit 1</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">TAMPERED</span>
          </div>
          Digest mismatch — the file has been modified after signing.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="danger">Exit 1</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">INVALID_CERT</span>
          </div>
          Certificate cannot be verified against the Fulcio root.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="danger">Exit 1</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">IDENTITY_MISMATCH</span>
          </div>
          Certificate SAN does not match the claimed signer.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="warning">Exit 2</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">UNSIGNED</span>
          </div>
          No sidecar file found. Not a hard failure by default.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="warning">Exit 3</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">POLICY_FAIL</span>
          </div>
          Signature is valid but does not meet the caller's trust policy.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="danger">Exit 1</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">SKILL_ID_MISMATCH</span>
          </div>
          Skill_id owner path doesn't match signer owner path.
        </bh-card>

        <bh-card variant="outlined" padding="md">
          <div slot="header">
            <bh-badge variant="danger">Exit 1</bh-badge>
            <span class="heading-sm" style="margin-left: var(--bh-spacing-2);">MALFORMED_SIDECAR</span>
          </div>
          Sidecar file is present but cannot be parsed or has invalid structure.
        </bh-card>
      </bh-grid>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section text-center">
    <h2 class="heading-lg">Ready to get started?</h2>
    <p class="text-muted" style="margin-top: var(--bh-spacing-2); margin-bottom: var(--bh-spacing-6);">
      Install SkillSign and sign your first skill in under a minute.
    </p>
    <bh-button variant="primary" size="lg" onclick={`window.location.href='${base}getting-started'`}>
      Quick Start Guide →
    </bh-button>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: var(--bh-spacing-20) var(--bh-spacing-6) var(--bh-spacing-12);
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .header-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--bh-text-lg);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin-top: var(--bh-spacing-4);
    line-height: var(--bh-leading-relaxed);
  }

  .section-inner {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .flow-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--bh-spacing-3) 0;
  }

  .flow-list li {
    padding: var(--bh-spacing-1) 0;
    padding-left: var(--bh-spacing-5);
    position: relative;
  }

  .flow-list li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--bh-color-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-header {
      padding: var(--bh-spacing-12) var(--bh-spacing-4) var(--bh-spacing-8);
    }
  }
</style>
